        "content": "# \ud83c\udfb4 Decked Out - Master Game Documentation\n\nWelcome to the **Decked Out** Knowledge Base. This vault documents the complete game design, mechanics, content compendium, and architectural implementation of *Decked Out*, a roguelike deck-building dungeon crawler built in **Godot 4.6**.\n\n```\n                           \u2554\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2557\n                           \u2551        DECKED OUT         \u2551\n                           \u2551 Roguelike Deck-Builder    \u2551\n                           \u255a\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u255d\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> \ud83c\udfa8 **Interactive Visual Board**: Open [[Decked Out - Master Canvas.canvas|Master Game Canvas]] to explore the entire game structure, heroes, cards, and systems visually!\n\n## \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f Map of Content (Quick Navigation)\n\n### 01. \u2694\ufe0f Core Gameplay & Systems\n- [[Game Overview & Pitch]] - Core concept, genre identity, and primary game loop.\n- [[Combat Mechanics]] - Turn sequence, mana, damage calculations, Armor, Ward, Speed, and DoTs.\n- [[Deck & Hand Rules]] - 100-card limits, 15-duplicate caps, draw phases, inter-act discard recycling, banish, and sideboard.\n- [[Dungeon Generation & Map]] - Three-Act procedural map (Act 1: 12, Act 2: 10, Act 3: 18 floors), unified Rest/Loot campsites, and The God.\n\n### 02. \ud83d\udcb0 Currencies, Economy & Gacha\n- [[Dual Currency System]] - Gold (In-Run Currency) vs. Gems (Out-Run Meta Currency) and Essence.\n- [[Booster Packs & Gacha]] - Pack tiers (Common, Rare, Exotic, Class, Bundle), drop rates, and first-time rewards.\n- [[In-Run Shop & Sideboard]] - Purchasing cards during runs, refresh costs, and the 5 substitute sideboard slots.\n\n### 03. \ud83c\udccf Card Compendium & Archetypes\n- [[Card System & Anatomy]] - Card stats, 6 rarity tiers, animated & alternate artwork, and resource attributes.\n- [[Card Classes & Archetypes]] - In-depth breakdown of Elixir, Wild Mages, Swordsman, Animal, Monster, and Goblins.\n- [[Series 1 Compendium]] - Comprehensive reference for all 72 cards in Series 1 (including the 15-card Goblins expansion).\n\n### 04. \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Heroes\n- [[Heroes Overview]] - Hero archetypes, baseline stats, unlock pathways, and scaling.\n- [[Deck Monk]] - The balanced, versatile starter hero.\n- [[Gorilla Gabe]] - The raw-power brawler with high HP and restricted mana.\n- [[Lost Spirit]] - Spectral glass-cannon with extra card draw and discard recursion.\n- [[Necri]] - Dark necromancer with Bone Ward, HP regen, and passive Skeleton summoning.\n- [[Demonling]] - Hellfire specialist with burn attacks and Demolitionist summoning.\n- [[Hunter The Hedgehog]] - Rapid skirmisher with all-enemy attacks, wound/bleed, and Quill summoning.\n- [[Scrap Goblin]] - Scavenger hero turning discarded cards into Scrap, fueling in-combat abilities & upgrades.\n\n### 05. \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f World & Encounters\n- [[Encounter Rooms Overview]] - Guide to all 12 dungeon room types.\n- [[The Trader]] - Card swapping, permanent card acquisition with Gems, and currency exchange.\n- [[The Chemist]] - Alchemical brewing, card essence extraction, and elixir fusion.\n- [[The Gambler]] - High-risk wagers, card gambling, and death-defying damage buffs.\n\n### 06. \ud83d\udc7e Enemies & Bosses\n- [[Enemy Stats & Scaling]] - AI action slots, floor stat scaling (+25% HP, +18% ATK), and elite multipliers.\n- [[Dungeon Enemies]] - Common and elite monsters spanning Bandits, Cultists, Beasts, and Automatons.\n- [[Boss - Dragon Lord]] - The climactic floor encounter and boss mechanics.\n\n### 07. \ud83d\udc8e Relics, Meta-Progression & Upgrades\n- [[Relics & The Relic Hub]] - 3 active relic slots, shard unlocking, and permanent passive artifacts.\n- [[Card & Hero Upgrades]] - Meta-spending Gems for +10% card stats and +3% hero stats.\n- [[Challenges & Unlocks]] - Quest achievements for unlocking heroes, bonus Gems, and milestones.\n- [[Difficulties & Modes]] - Easy, Normal, Hard, Expert, and Nightmare difficulty tiers.\n\n### 08. \ud83d\udcbb Engine & Architecture\n- [[Godot Project Architecture]] - Autoload singletons (`GameManager`, `PackManager`, `AudioManager`), save files, and scene routing.\n- [[Soundtrack & Audio Design]] - Original music tracks, ambient soundscapes, and combat SFX.\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Use Obsidian's **Graph View** (`Ctrl + G`) to see the rich web of connections between Heroes, Cards, Relics, and Systems!"
