        "content": "# \ud83d\udcbc The Trader\n\n> *\"Got goods, got deals. If you have the coin or gems, everything is negotiable.\"*\n\n**The Trader** (`TraderScene.gd`) is an elite traveling merchant who appears along branching dungeon paths (4.0% spawn rate, max 2 times per run, Floor 4+). Unlike standard in-run card shops, the Trader offers advanced barter, permanent unlocks, and currency exchanges.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Available Services\n\n### 1. Card Barter (Fair Trade System)\n- The Trader displays a rotating stock of **4 to 6 rare cards** (weighted towards Uncommon, Rare, Epic, and Legendary) using full card visuals.\n- Players can trade away an unwanted card from their active run deck to obtain one of the Trader's high-tier cards.\n- **Fair Surcharge**: Trading up in rarity incurs a Gold fee to prevent exploiting starter cards:\n  - Same or lower rarity: 15 Gold exchange fee\n  - +1 Rarity (e.g. Common \u2794 Uncommon): +30 Gold\n  - +2 Rarity (e.g. Common \u2794 Rare): +65 Gold\n  - +3 Rarity (e.g. Common \u2794 Epic): +110 Gold\n  - +4 Rarity (e.g. Common \u2794 Legendary): +160 Gold\n\n### 2. Permanent Card Unlock (Buy with Gems)\n- Spot a card during your run that you love and want to keep forever in your binder?\n- The Trader allows you to pay **Gems (ORC)** to permanently add that card to your save slot's persistent collection:\n  - Base Cost: **100 Gems** (scales upward with card rarity: Uncommon 200, Rare 300, Epic 500, Legendary 800, Exotic 1200).\n\n### 3. Currency Exchange\nNeed Gems for meta-progression or desperate for Gold to survive?\n- **Sell Gold for Gems**: `150 Gold \u2794 100 Gems` (1.5:1 ratio).\n- **Sell Gems for Gold**: `100 Gems \u2794 50 Gold` (2:1 ratio).\n- **Visit Limit**: Up to 3 exchanges per visit.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Tactical Utility\n\n- **Deck Purging & Refinement**: Use the Trader to swap out redundant starter cards for game-winning Epic or Legendary powerhouses without breaking the run economy.\n- **Collection Acceleration**: Target-farm rare cards without relying solely on booster pack RNG.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd17 Related Notes\n- [[Dual Currency System]]\n- [[Encounter Rooms Overview]]\n- [[In-Run Shop & Sideboard]]"
